From b96a1ea5c87b1c882d035613461af9e155f207ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verif <h3@verif>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:40:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Gate 6: undo two Ibex specialisations that are not
 architectural

1. legalize_tvec / legalize_mcause: restore upstream riscv/sail-riscv's
   generic WARL behaviour, parameterised on a writable-bit mask whose
   default (all ones) reproduces upstream bit-for-bit.

   lowRISC replaced upstream's legalize_tvec with Mk_Mtvec(v[31..8] @ 0x01)
   -- 256-byte aligned BASE, MODE hardwired to vectored -- and ADDED a
   legalize_mcause (upstream has none; writeCSR does mcause.bits = value)
   carrying Ibex's internal-interrupt encoding.  mtvec and mcause are WARL
   registers; both lowRISC policies and Hazard3's are legal implementations
   of the same architecture, so the choice belongs in configuration.

2. LOAD / STORE: restore upstream's check_misaligned call.  lowRISC's memory
   rework (b63cba3c) deleted it along with translateAddr / mem_write_ea,
   which left check_misaligned defined but never called and
   plat_enable_misaligned_access dead configuration; the model then split
   every misaligned access into two granules regardless of the platform
   flag.  Misaligned support is optional in RISC-V, so which of trap and
   split the model does is exactly what that flag is for.

Baseline: lowrisc/sail-riscv 81a266b6 (branch ibex), the revision pinned by
ibex's flake.lock, byte-identical to $LOWRISC_SAIL_RISCV_SRC.
---
 model/riscv_insts_base.sail  | 21 ++++++++++--
 model/riscv_insts_zicsr.sail |  2 +-
 model/riscv_sys_regs.sail    | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

